\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf3 \strokec3 \
Figure 1 Study pipeline: Identify -> Predict -> Actuate with the minimal observation set\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Identify
\f1\b0  \'97 the censoring identifiability analysis (Section 3.3.1), a 90-cycle paired validation, and a mixed-occupancy three-estimator ablation (naive / quota-scaled / throttle-corrected).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Predict
\f1\b0  \'97 the density law $N^* = C/(\\varphi + (1-\\varphi)\\rho) = C/(\\rho\\kappa)$; three-point mixed-phase validation, the anti-phase arrangement experiment, and threshold-qualified capacity curves (primary bar P5 \uc0\u8805  70%).\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Actuate
\f1\b0  \'97 risk-calibrated admission (pseudocode and calibration protocol in Section 5.3.1) landing on the capacity oracle in an online head-to-head comparison; no-regression controls (KSM/FPR/zram, adaptive IO; micro-period quotas re-measured \'97 the earlier +35% claim is withdrawn, Section 9.1) raising density per resource.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 1.4 Summary of Results\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Identify
\f1\b0 : five pegged tenants at 30% quota show 1.50 cores on the usage panel against 5.00 cores of true demand (3.3x, 7/7 rounds); in the v2 repeat (50% quota), throttle-corrected estimates hit the truth in all 90 cycles and naive "release" decisions violate in 
\f0\b 90/90
\f1\b0 ; the v3 rework (30% quota, 90 cycles) replicates the direction (naive 3.6x under-report; corrected median |err| 0.55 cores, 88/90 within \'b120%); a mixed-occupancy ablation (3 pegged + 3 idle @30%, truth 3.3) yields aggregate errors \'97 naive -2.31 (unsafe), quota-scaling +0.01 (smallest 
\f2\i in this sample
\f1\i0  because bursty peaks saturate the quota), throttle correction -0.20, full-vCPU +2.70, uncapped -0.16 \'97 while per tenant, saturated tenants are exact under both methods and the window-averaged throttle fraction is diluted by idle time for bursty tenants (0.033 vs true 0.10); estimator choice must rest on per-tenant correctness, with multi-resolution throttle sequences (Ch. 9) fixing the dilution.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Predict
\f1\b0 : the density law hits three mixed-phase break points on the physical host \'97 $\\varphi$=0.50 predicted 13.3 (13 pass, 16 fail), $\\varphi$=0.75 predicted 10.0 (10 pass, 13 fail), $\\varphi$=0.25 predicted 20.0 (20\'9624 pass, 28 fail); random-vs-aligned safe capacity ratio 3.5\'d7 at the primary bar (3.5\'d7\'964\'d7 across bars); the utilization-impossibility counterexample (35% vs 98%).\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Actuate
\f1\b0 : isolation is the only lever surviving every storm (physical-core verified); the fixed phase-aware admission stops 
\f0\b inside the fine-scanned synchronized bracket (8 seats; 10 = first fail)
\f1\b0 ; KSM reclaims 
\f0\b 21.4 GiB (33.4% of fleet RAM)
\f1\b0  with service P99 0.73\uc0\u8594 0.76 ms, and idle "1 GB" VMs hold only 156\'96315 MB of host memory (free-page reporting already returning free pages) \'97 the key enabler of memory density.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Evidence strength
\f1\b0 : 100-round knee (two batches), 180-cycle censoring (two batches), 30-round combined-stress campaign, 4-round fine scan, 3-round sync; explicit statistics (round-clustered, binomial bounds, P99 primary), anomalies (OOM-offline VMs, degraded rounds, batch drift) archived and merged via the v3 rework.\
