\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \strokec2 Raising the service VMs' 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 cpu.weight
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  to 1000 (10\'d7) and 10000 (100\'d7, a verification run) against default-100 tenants under five pegged tenants yields service P99 25.4/22.8 and 24.0/22.7 ms \'97 
\f0\b worse than no weights at all
\f1\b0  (historic five-pegged P99 21.6/19.5 ms) and opposite to the intuition that weights favor the service. IO weights (
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 io.weight
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  50 vs 500) are equally inert. 
\f0\b Soft priorities are not tail-latency protections; isolation is.
\f1\b0 \
