\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Correlation correction.
\f1\b0  Rounds share host state (long-run drift, caches, same-batch VM state), so independence is an optimistic bound; the protocol requires (i) effective sample size computed by time-block/round clustering, reporting effective < nominal rounds; (ii) block-level worst-window sensitivity; (iii) every "zero-violation" statement carries its round count and bound.\

\f0\b Scope of the protocol.
\f1\b0  This protocol defines how safety statements must be phrased and what evidence they carry; it is not itself a guarantee. The experiments reported in this paper state their round counts and measured bounds explicitly (e.g., 29/30 envelope passes carry an optimistic one-sided bound of ~14.9%) and do not constitute a 1% risk certificate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

