\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.1 Testbed\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 The testbed is a nested host isomorphic to small-provider production: Proxmox VE 8.4.21 (Debian 12 base) running inside a KVM guest (
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 systemd-detect-virt = kvm
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 ; 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 /dev/kvm
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  and 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 vmx/svm
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  both available), reporting 4 vCPUs (AMD EPYC 9575F), 19.5 GiB of RAM, one 200 GB virtual disk (cgroup accounting device 8:0), and 1 GB of swap. Ballooning is disabled by default (the return-vs-no-compression tradeoff, Section 4.4.4). The host's idle baseline is 2\'964% busy; all background noise is removed during experiments (a local monitoring agent and per-VM apt/man-db/fstrim timers are disabled).\
Load topology: 2 service VMs (HTTP/nginx, Redis; 1 vCPU / 1 GiB each), 1 probe VM, and 16 customer VMs (1 vCPU, 3072 MiB; some earlier experiments used 1024/5120 MiB, noted per section). All VMs are clones of one Debian 12 cloud template (cloud-init injects networking and keys); customer VMs carry no persistent agents.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

