\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.3 Use of AI-Assisted Tools\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 AI assistants were used for language editing, code review and manuscript organization during preparation. All experiment design and execution, data verification and scientific claims are the author's own; every reported number was checked against the archived raw logs (see Statements and Declarations).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.4 Read-Only Production Telemetry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 The two production hosts are monitored read-only and anonymously: PVE read-only interfaces (
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 pvesh get /nodes
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 , 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 /nodes/\{node\}/status
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 , 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 /cluster/resources
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 ) plus 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 /proc
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  provide CPU service volume, throttle counters, pressure signals, memory, and lifecycle events at 60-second granularity for a 7-day target. The remote collector HMAC-pseudonymizes VM/node IDs in memory; it never collects VM names, IPs, business content, or disk data; it installs nothing, changes no customer quota, and applies no stress. Credentials are used once for key exchange and discarded; keys live only on the researcher's workstation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 6.5 Reproducibility\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Testbed scripts, all raw data (219 raw files, 34 JSONL logs, analysis scripts), and the experimental protocol are archived with the paper; the data dictionary (fields, units, semantics, quality flags) and an execution log (every environment change and anomaly) are included. All violation determinations use the pre-registered SLO and window definitions; rejected candidates are never started, and evaluation inputs retain their planned demand \'97 there is no post-hoc selection of runs.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 7 Evaluation\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\ri480\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf3 \strokec3 Three evaluation groups: (A) admission-policy comparison; (B) shaping and protection-envelope comparison; (C) combined-stress synthesis validation, followed by the production-telemetry usage and an explicit gap list. Common SLO: service P99 \uc0\u8804  10 ms.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 \strokec2 7.1 Setup Recap\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Testbed and metrics: Sections 3\'964 and 7. Admission comparisons use a closed loop: five candidate tenants arrive one at a time, a policy decides allow/defer from evidence visible at that moment, and allowed candidates are actually started and measured. Shaping comparisons use the neighbor sweep (0\'965 tenants) plus the full combined-stress. Every key conclusion replicates at least twice (knee: 5 rounds; censoring: 7 cycles; synthesis: 4 passes).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

