\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Reading.
\f1\b0  Both decisions consume the same data and differ only in estimation: naive takes censored usage as demand and hallucinates half the host as empty; aware pins the demand lower bound above the quota using throttle evidence. The former action pushes the host into instantaneous saturation (tenants at 27\'9632 M it/s, host at 100%); the latter avoids the self-inflicted wound and emits the correct capacity signal. We keep the detail that the quota state itself sits near the SLO line: 
\f0\b this host is already at the overload boundary, and the upper action (migrate/upgrade) is out of scope here.
\f1\b0 \
