\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Reading.
\f1\b0  Only isolation raises the safe limit (to \uc0\u8805 5); quotas change tenant speed, not the limit (Section 4.4.1). The cost relocation is visible: isolation moves the cost from "service SLO" to "economy-tier customers", while quotas satisfy neither side. The remaining defenses \'97 memory double gate and IO caps \'97 do not raise the CPU knee but stop their own storms from dragging the service under (they are necessary parts of the synthesis configuration).\
