\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Three conclusions.
\f1\b0  (i) the phase-aware controller is the only one combining the aligned-phase 8-seat bracket with competitive random-phase capacity (16\'9620; worstcase/quantile stop at 8 in 
\f2\i both
\f1\i0  phases, fixed at 16 in both; the fine scan pins the aligned boundary at [8,10): 10 seats give customer P5=62.2%, first fail); (ii) utilization-based criteria are quantified as phase-dependent: util80 sells 28 (safe) under random and 40 (customer P5 collapses to 16%) under aligned \'97same policy, same hardware, opposite risk; audible-style collapses likewise; (iii) fixed and worstcase/quantile verify the other two corners. Safe VM-hours and round-level intervals from the show4/show5 repeats are reported above where available.\

\f0\b Sampling caveat:
\f1\b0  the earlier sync rounds have a probe-before-rates ordering defect that pushed rate sampling out of the burst window (audible/util80 happen to have valid violation evidence via phase drift; fixed etc. lack the p5 column); the corrected seven-round rerun (show5) was completed and the sync customer columns are reported via the four-round ladder.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 7.4.2 Repeat, Ablation, and Sensitivity Checks (show6-show12)\
