\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Reading.
\f1\b0  (i) Pinning and caps keep the service safe: zero violations under both policies \'97 in joint operation the admission policy decides 
\f2\i how many seats are committed
\f1\i0 , not service safety. (ii) The dominant customer-side pain comes from the tight memory gate: the canary's multi-second stalls are nearly identical at 1 and 3 seats, showing that 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 memory.high = 800 MB
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  is too tight for a 3 GB guest (cf. the soft-threshold semantics of Section 4.4.4); the economy tier's experience ceiling is a product parameter, not a policy defect. (iii) Throttle-corrected estimation carries a phase bias: with bursty background, instant sampling at decision time underestimates demand (estimates oscillated between 0.01 and 1.90 cores), making the aware policy over-conservative (1 seat vs naive's 3) \'97 the design-to-implementation gap versus the time-aligned aggregate upper quantile of Section 5.3, tracked as an improvement item. The revision implements the time-aligned aggregation; it is re-measured as a four-policy comparison on the second testbed, with results merged as supplementary material.\
