\f0\b \cf2 Unit check.
\f1\b0  Sum of guest 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 cpu
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  x vCPUs = 15.3 cores ~ host counter busy = 14.8 cores; the single-core reading gives only 10.2 cores \'97 the guest 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 cpu
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  field is confirmed as 
\f0\b fraction of allocated vCPU
\f1\b0 , consistent at host level.\

\f0\b Portrait (Figure 27).
\f1\b0  Classes: idle (<5%) 71.9%, light (5\'9630%) 27.1%, heavy (>30%) 1.0%, matching the "mostly idle, a few heavy" modeling premise. Oversubscription anchors: 5.76x vCPU oversubscription (configured vCPUs over 50 cores), 1.12x memory-limit oversubscription, and about 95 GiB of actual memory in use \'97 the testbed's 5x scale comes from real practice, not inflation. Burst structure: 4268 active runs (>=5% consecutive), median 1 minute, 3550 of them single-minute, short bursts dominate; value-level autocorrelation is ~0 across 1\'9630 min, so there is no minute-scale persistence and no clock period, while the state layer persists (Markov self-transitions 0.85/0.37/0.26) \'97 real bursts are runs of varying length with drifting phase, neither i.i.d. nor clocked. Saturated instances (>=95% vCPU) occupy 0.046% of VM-samples: genuinely heavy tenants are rare but present.\

\f0\b Implications.
\f1\b0  (i) A 1% heavy class plus instantaneous overlap is the entire risk source \'97 echoing the Chapter 4 result that a single pegged neighbor collapses the tail; (ii) real bursts drift rather than tick: the synthetic "strict 60 s alignment" is a 
\f0\b worst-case upper bound
\f1\b0 , so the mixed-phase model's $\\varphi$should be read low on production hosts and safe capacity sits near the random end \'97 consistent with 5.76x oversubscription running in the field; (iii) the read-only interface lacks throttle counters, so the censoring share is proxied by the saturated-instance fraction as a lower bound; (iv) 
\f0\b inter-tenant correlation (minute granularity)
\f1\b0 : 204 active VMs, 20706 pairs, mean Pearson r = 0.12, median 0.07, P95 0.45, 15.7% of pairs above 0.3 \'97
\f2\i weakly positive, not independent
\f1\i0 : phase structure is not an artifact of synthetic loads, while the random-end assumption of the capacity model is only an approximation; sub-minute synchrony stays invisible at this granularity. (v) 
\f0\b Two-window representativeness:
\f1\b0  the 3-h dense excerpt is a night-time quiet segment (busy 30.1%), while the 42-h light window covers day and night (busy 37.3%, peak 66.1%) - the "mostly idle" portrait is a per-VM statement; host-level load follows a day/night rhythm, and capacity-model anchors taken from the quiet segment are labeled as such (the controlled experiments here align with that segment; day/night peak regimes are future work).\

\f0\b Second production host (OVH ns503701).
\f1\b0  A 6-hour dense window (60 s samples, 344 points) on a second, independent production host: Xeon E5-1630 v4 (4 cores / 8 threads, 62.7 GiB RAM; swap nearly full at inventory time) with 
\f0\b 66 running guests, sum vCPU 73 (9.1x)
\f1\b0 ; host busy mean 
\f0\b 30.9%
\f1\b0  (peak 44.6%); CPU PSI (some) avg300 7.2 mean / 8.2 peak, PSI (full) 0.0 throughout; guest CPU consumption 1.84 of 8 threads (23%); node memory in use 43.3 of 62.7 GiB (69%); heavy share (>=30% of a vCPU) 2.2%. The portrait reproduces the HK structure at similar density: 
\f0\b 9-12x vCPU oversubscription coexisting with a mostly-idle host and zero full-stall pressure
\f1\b0 , corroborating that the testbed's scale and the "mostly idle, a few heavy" premise are drawn from field practice.\

\f0\b Boundaries and the two-state anchor (Figure 31).
\f1\b0  The dense window is only 170 minutes and is a
\f0\b night-time quiet segment
\f1\b0  (host busy 30.1%, peak 47.2%); the light stream has accumulated 
\f0\b 42 hours of day/night coverage
\f1\b0  (as of 2026-10-14; 305 points at 5-minute intervals, ~39% of samples missing to relay jitter): host busy mean 
\f0\b 37.3%
\f1\b0 , P95 55.3%, peak 
\f0\b 66.1%
\f1\b0 ; guests consume 14.8%of host CPU on average; memory available never drops below 
\f0\b 63.7 GB
\f1\b0 ; CPU PSI avg300 mean 5.2, peak 14.0; no reboot in the window. The two-state anchor holds: the quiet/night dense segment (to which the controlled testbed experiments align) and the full day/night light segment together bracket the real load range. 1-minute granularity cannot resolve sub-minute synchrony.\
