\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \strokec2 The model (an approximation under explicit assumptions, not a universal law).
\f1\b0  Assumptions: (A1) tenant phases are stable within the decision span; (A2) the aligned group's bursts coincide, and overlap with random tenants follows duty. Under these, the aggregate concurrency peak is \uc0\u8776  aligned group $\\varphi N$ +random group $\\rho(1-\\varphi)N$, giving the median-bar capacity\
$$N^*_\{\\text\{mid\}\} \\;\\approx\\; \\frac\{C\}\{\\varphi + (1-\\varphi)\\,\\rho\},$$\
i.e., the concentration form $N^*_\{\\text\{mid\}\} = C/(\\rho\\kappa)$. 
\f0\b The model describes the mean/median bar; at the pure-random end it is markedly optimistic for the P5 tail bar
\f1\b0  (model 40 vs measured 28). The random-end tail is naturally governed by the upper quantile of overlap counts: require$Q_p(\\varphi N + \\mathrm\{Bin\}((1-\\varphi)N, \\rho)) \\le C/\\theta$; numerically this sits below the median bar. In practice the safe value is taken directly from the 
\f0\b measured
\f1\b0  bar-qualified capacity (\'a78.4), and the model is used only for cross-configuration extrapolation and as the admission prior.\

