\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 \strokec2 9.1 CPU: Micro-Period Quotas \'97 a Self-Audit Correction (Figure 22)\
\pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \pard\pardeftab720\qc\partightenfactor0

\fs25\fsmilli12667 \cf3 \strokec3 \
Figure 22 Micro-period self-audit: 2 ms and 1 s deliver identically (+35% withdrawn)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 \strokec2 Background.
\f1\b0  An early batch (qp2c: five pegged tenants at 50% quota, periods 2/4/10/100 ms/1 s) reported that shrinking the period raised the tenant rate from 59% to 80% (+35%), and this number entered the summary table.\

\f0\b Audit and correction (qp2v1).
\f1\b0  A pre-submission measurement audit found that qp2c's rate readings come from the burner's 
\f0\b cumulative average within the current work phase
\f1\b0  (rewritten every ~2 s), while configs were only ~30 s apart \'97 so 
\f0\b later configs read windows contaminated by earlier, faster ones
\f1\b0  (the uncapped segment at 25.6M inflated early readings). Clean re-measurement: fresh burner window per config + synchronized 60 s windows + guest 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 cpu.stat
