\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 10 Discussion and Limitations\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 10.1 What Transfers, What Is Environment-Bound\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Mechanistic results that transfer:
\f1\b0  (i) tail latency is governed by instantaneous concurrency/overlap rather than average utilization \'97 independent of core count and virtualization depth, depending only on whether the runnable set periodically exceeds capacity; (ii) the censoring logic \'97 any system whose self-protection uses quotas will let usage underestimate demand, and throttle counters are a portable detector; (iii) the reliability hierarchy \'97 isolation > hard caps > soft priorities, with the failures of the latter having mechanism-level explanations (lock-holder preemption, scheduling-credit dynamics, upstream dispatch) rather than being testbed accidents.\

\f0\b Environment-bound numbers:
\f1\b0  the "3\uc0\u8594 4" knee is specific to 4 logical cores with 1-core pegged tenants as the worst case; the memory cliff (~13.8 GB tenant residency with 1 GB swap) is bound to 19.5 GiB physical and the swap layout; IO numbers are bound to the virtual disk and the host's 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 none
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  scheduler (no BFQ). The paper reports mechanisms and the relative limit\'96cost relation; readers should recompute absolute numbers for their own cores and reserves.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 10.2 SLO Tiers and the Capacity\'96Quality Curve\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 All experiments use the strict tier P99 \uc0\u8804  10 ms. Real cheap-VPS customers have no formal SLO and typically tolerate tens of milliseconds; our own data show that the same ten-tenant mix that violates the 10 ms tier would mostly be fine at ~30 ms. 
\f0\b "How much can be sold" is therefore a function of the SLO tier, not a constant
\f1\b0  \'97 providers should make the density\'96tier relation an explicit product parameter , e.g., economy tier P99 \uc0\u8804  50 ms, standard \u8804  20 ms instead of quietly holding everyone to the strictest tier. The sensitivity analysis is on the pre-submission list; the mechanism and initial data are in place.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 10.3 Design Implications\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 For providers: 
\f0\b isolation first, density second
\f1\b0  \'97 one dedicated core for sensitive workloads beats any parameter tuning; backstop memory and IO with the double gate and caps; state the nominal sales envelope separately from the protection envelope (the basis for tiered pricing); feed admission with evidence (throttle counters, time-aligned demand upper quantiles) rather than dashboard numbers. For platform builders: several "intuitive" cgroup v2 semantics need empirical calibration \'97 IO accounting binds to the whole disk rather than the partition; 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 io.weight
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  depends on the IO scheduler being one that honors it (the IO-cost route 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 io.cost.*
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  exists but was not exercised here); 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 memory.high
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  reclaim pressure spills into host swap unless paired with 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 memory.swap.max
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  (or swap disabled), and as a soft threshold it is not an OOM exemption; CPU weight is not a latency-protection tool. These gaps deserve documentation and default-configuration fixes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 10.4 Validity and Threats\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 Construct validity.
\f1\b0  The "business" services are lightweight HTTP/Redis stand-ins; real services (databases, gateways) have longer and more syscall-dependent paths, which change absolute numbers but not the structure of overlap-driven tails. Tenant loads are synthetic duty-cycle loops without real-application slow paths (lock contention, GC); replication with real application images is future work.
\f0\b Internal validity.
\f1\b0  Nested virtualization adds a scheduling layer; randomized orders and replicates suppress noise, and service-side metrics are stable across synthesis passes. The weight-failure mechanism is not yet localized (a host-side packet-path hypothesis is unverified) and is kept as an open question. The joint validation exposed a further issue: instant sampling of bursty background load carries a phase bias, the full controller (phase profiles + censoring correction + pause guardrail) is implemented and evaluated in the online comparison (Section 7.4.1; the j1 joint pilot is kept as a historical design\'96implementation gap record); the customer-side canary shows that a tight 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 memory.high
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333  gate can cause multi-second stalls, so gate sizing must be an explicitly calibrated product parameter.
\f0\b Control-history boundary (preliminary pilot).
\f1\b0  The observation set validated in this paper is sufficient for capacity decisions under the tested workload family, but it does not identify work-preservation semantics. In a controlled paired pilot (one replaceable/latest-state tenant vs one persistent-queue tenant, matched baseline telemetry of 0.80 vs 0.83 cores, identical 20% quota for 3 min, then release), the throttled-phase host telemetry of the two tenants is indistinguishable (0.200 vs 0.200 cores; throttled 143.2 vs 143.2 s), yet the released futures differ sharply: the replaceable tenant returns to baseline immediately with a recovery ratio kappa = E/D = 0.004 (discarded work never returns), while the persistent tenant stays saturated for about 12 min draining the accumulated debt, kappa = 0.975. Host-side history collected before a control action therefore cannot predict the post-action load for both semantics; evidence validity after control actions is an open boundary of the observation-necessity thesis, and a multi-workload, multi-run study is future work (artifacts: 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 research_data/debt_pilot/
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 ; model-level executable counterexamples in 
\f3\fs28\fsmilli14107 tools/control_history_tests.py
\f1\fs30\fsmilli15333 ).\

\f0\b External validity.
\f1\b0  Two testbeds (a 4-vCPU nested bed and a 96-thread bare-metal host) with production telemetry as a realistic anchor; the production-schedule replay (64 real per-minute duty traces; 30-min excerpt plus five-window forward validation) has been run (Section 8.6); production telemetry is minute-level, so the multi-window PPC validation uses 
\f2\i reconstructed
\f1\i0  second-level series (model-replay consistency) \'97 independent second-level truth and false-positive/negative rates remain future work; cross-vendor hardware extrapolation remains a follow-up item.
\f0\b Statistics.
\f1\b0  Key conclusions carry mass repeats (knee 50, censoring 90 cycles in 30 rounds, combined-stress 24); the admission comparison v2 (14 rounds), boundary fine scans (multi-cycle, 2 rounds per step) and mixed-phase repeats are running; zero-failure claims are reported with Clopper-Pearson bounds and explicit trial counts, never as long-term guarantees.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 10.5 Boundary to Hyperscale Approaches\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 This work does not replace AUDIBLE/Coach-class methods at hyperscale, which solve capacity optimization given long histories and scheduling freedom; it addresses how a history-less, migration-less small host avoids incidents when its measurement interface is structurally biased. The two are composable: censoring correction can produce clean demand evidence at the small-host edge before a platform-scale predictor performs global planning.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 11 Conclusion\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs30\fsmilli15333 \cf2 This paper targets an operating regime overlooked by large-scale cloud research \'97 small VPS hosts that pack cheap, mostly-idle, occasionally-bursty tenants into a few physical cores \'97 and, using 
\f0\b two self-built testbeds
\f1\b0  (a 4-vCPU nested bed and a 96-thread bare-metal host whose 64-VM fleet reproduces the core results, with isolation verified against SMT/NUMA topology), 
\f0\b mass repeats at the 50/90/24-round scale
\f1\b0  and read-only telemetry from two production hosts we operate ourselves, recasts "safe oversubscription" as three ordered problems whose organizing thesis is 
\f0\b observation necessity
\f1\b0  (Section 3.6): censoring identification, phase resolution and time resolution are each necessary \'97 with (1)(2) directly measured and (3) currently a construction plus indirect evidence \'97 and jointly sufficient as an empirical statement for our target workload family (the policy with all three is the only one in the 14-round comparison combining random-phase capacity (16\'9620 seats) with the aligned-phase 8-seat stop and random-phase customer compliance; aligned-phase customer P5 ~99% at 8 seats, 4-round ladder).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\qj\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 Identify.
\f1\b0  Quota censoring makes demand unobservable in aggregate counters: the point estimate equals the running-stretch mean (exact iff the two stretch means agree; constant demand is sufficient but not necessary), the floor q(1+t) is conditional (and, following the counterexample above, explicitly an empirical conservative heuristic rather than a certified bound), and aggregate non-identifiability is constructed. Validation across 90 cycles (30 independent rounds, clustered) shows throttle-corrected estimates match the truth while naive release decisions violate in 90/90; the mixed-occupancy ablation quantifies all five estimators (naive -2.31, quota-scaling +0.01 by coincidence, throttle correction -0.20, full-vCPU +2.70, uncapped -0.16) and isolates the window-dilution effect that multi-resolution throttle sequences will fix.\

\f0\b Predict.
\f1\b0  Capacity is set by phase structure, not average utilization: random vs aligned safe capacity 28 vs 8 (primary bar P5 \uc0\u8805  70%; 3.5x\'964x across bars), with the utilization-impossibility counterexample \'97 and the measured inversion (safe fleet reports 66.4-68.0% busy, the collapsing fleet 30.4%). The safe-capacity approximation N* = C/(phi + (1-phi) rho) is stated with explicit assumptions and measured error directions. The Phase-Profile Convolution (PPC) has three artifact-backed modes (parametric simulation, strict three-way joint block bootstrap with a held-out test third, online peak-envelope approximation); iid convolution is provably blind to exactly the axis that decides safety (the marginal illusion), and the C5 intervention shows the axis is controllable (capacity x2/x4 by phase arrangement alone).\

\f0\b Actuate.
\f1\b0  In the complete 14-round comparison (identical arrival streams and evidence), the phase-aware admission is the only policy combining the verified aligned-phase bracket (8 seats, customer P5 ~99%) with competitive random-phase capacity (16\'9620); the audible-style and busy-threshold baselines sell 40 in the aligned phase and collapse customer P5 to 16%, and the fixed-oversubscription baseline violates the primary bar at 16 \'97 the phase-blindness of independence assumptions and of utilization criteria, quantified end to end. On the resource-efficiency side (supporting extension, Chapter 9), balloon-free reclaim (KSM 33.4% of fleet RAM; free-page reporting reclaiming 303 MB; zram absorbing 176.8 GB of overflow) raises density without shrinking tenant-visible resources under the 
\f0\b domain-scoped
\f1\b0  no-regression definition; micro-period quotas, IO storms and the QoE canary each carry a gain / hidden-cost / visible-regression ledger.\

\f0\b Limitations.
\f1\b0  Two testbeds, one bare-metal host; synthetic duty-cycle loads dominate, with the production-schedule replay (30-minute real schedule plus five-window forward validation) as a scenario anchor; real mixed application workloads and more arrival-order repeats remain future work; round-level ranges are reported throughout, and the formal bootstrap intervals will be refreshed on the frozen data set. "Jointly sufficient" remains an empirical statement for our target workload family. The study provides small VPS providers with a reproducible "observation design + capacity model + controller" starting point, and adds "identifiability boundaries and phase structure" to the oversubscription research agenda.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs40 \cf2 \strokec2 Appendix A \'97 Formal Statements and Executable Checks\
\pard\pardeftab720\li480\fi-480\ri480\sa213\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs28 \cf3 \strokec3 Companion to Sections 3.3.1 (Proposition A) and 3.6 (Propositions B1/B2/C). All constructions are numerically re-checked by 
\f3\fs25\fsmilli12880 tools/theory_tests.py
\f1\fs28  (output archived in 
